                <pb facs="0675" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg579"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 1 in No.
                    187.—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">republic of hayti, section of foreign
                        affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Le
                                Comité d’Ordre Public</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-19"><hi rendition="#italic">July 19, 1879</hi></date>—<hi
                            rendition="#italic">76th of the Independence.</hi></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">Liberty! Equality! Fraternity!</p>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: In consequence of the retirement
                    from the executive power of the President of Hayti, a committee of public order
                    has been found to fill a vacancy of the executive power until the government may
                    be reconstituted.</p>
                <p>The committee makes haste to inform you of this state of things and to give you
                    the assurance of its profound desire to maintain the good relations which exist
                    so happily between the government you represent and the Government of Hayti.</p>
                <p>The committee has been divided into bureaus for the expedition of the public
                    service; the bureau of foreign affairs is authorized to establish with you those
                    relations for which you are accredited near the Haytian Government.</p>
                <p>The bureau of foreign relations is superintended by Mr. Senator Denis. The
                    committee prays you, Mr. Minister, to accept, with its cordial salutations, the
                    assurance of its distinguished sentiments.</p>
                <closer>President:<lb/><signed>DENIS.</signed><lb/>Vice-President:
                        <signed>DÉLORME.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
